A||||3||WisconsinGT||Hedliner question.||||1||
Z||000000||WisconsinGT||08-04-2000||06:29 PM||||My weekend project will be putting in a new headliner. My question is what color am I looking for? I have an 88GT with the grey interior. I thought charcoal grey would be the color, but it looks like it is to dark. Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Gokart||08-04-2000||09:23 PM||||If your doing it this weekend I guess that won't give you enough time to do what I did and order a roll from JC Whitney. It was an exact match and it's tricot(foam backed)so I didn't have to worry about the contact cement bleeding through. If you decide to order and wait the part # is on this page <A HREF="http://www.castlegate.net/personals/daveheld/TechArt/headlinr.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.castlegate.net/personals/daveheld/TechArt/headlinr.htm</A>  I suggest you put a couple of coats of polyurethane on the board when you get it out too cause it makes it rigid and not prone to crumble on you when you go to put it back in. Be careful not to trim the fabric around the sunroof opening (if you have a sunroof) because you need excess there to pull into the recess area then putting in the plastic trim that holds in place. Good luck!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Gokart_sig_1.gif"> <P>Marc                     87GT||||reg||2
Z||000002||Phil||08-04-2000||10:53 PM||||I went to my local auto top place and bought 1 yd. of material. He had all types and colors, he even gave me some glue. Total cost $15.||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||08-05-2000||05:11 PM||||any fabric shops like Hancock Fabrics, ect carry it. It only comes in about a 1/2 dozen colors. Its sold with a lite foam backing attached to it. Its known in the auto trade as 'J&S' fabric. Of course if you want to make your car different you could look at all the other fabrics while your there. J&S only cost about $6 or $7 a yard<BR>||||reg||1
